# Cloudflare Pages natively serves /audit.html as both /audit (HTTP 200) and
# /audit.html (308 → /audit) via its auto-strip-html behavior, so no explicit
# alias is needed. (Adding one creates a redirect loop because the alias
# target gets stripped again.)

# SPA fallback: any URL that doesn't match a real file falls through to
# index.html so the client-side router can take over.
/*        /index.html   200
